<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss set terms on 3-month money market claims.</title>
<headline>Swiss set terms on 3-month money market claims.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss federal government announced that its latest series 3.361 of three-month money market claims will yield 1.629 percent.</p>
<p>The allocation of 966.15 million Swiss francs has a uniform price of 99.59 percent.</p>
<p>Payment is set for November 21.</p>
<p>The previous issue of three-month claims, series 3.360, paid for on November 14, raised 916.85 million francs and was priced at 99.598 to yield 1.597 percent.</p>
<p>-- Zurich editorial, +41 1 258 7340</p>
</text>
